主要终点:
To evaluate the safety and tolerability of P2203 injection.

The safety and tolerability of P2203 injection are evaluated by the occurrence of the adverse events, serious adverse events, and the abnormal clinical laboratory data, ECG changes, physical examination findings, and lab examinations.

from day 1 to day 36

To determine the maximum tolerated dose of P2203

The maximum tolerated dose is defined as the highest tolerated dose level without the occurrence of predetermined unacceptable safety scenario during the 28-day safety monitoring period. Unacceptable safety scenario includes:

* ≥ 1 of 6 subjects in Cohort 1 or ≥ 1 of 12 subjects in Cohort 2a experiences SAE(s) which is at least possibly related to P2203;
* ≥ 2 of 6 subjects in Cohort 1 or ≥ 2 of 12 subjects in Cohort 2a have severe (Grade 3 or higher as per CTCAE) non-serious adverse events which is at least possibly related to P2203;
* ≥ 2 of 6 subjects in Cohort 1 or ≥ 2 of 12 subjects in Cohort 2a have a drug related QTc pro-longation defined as QTcF \> 500 ms, or an increase of QTcF \> 60 ms above baseline on the 12-lead electrocardiogram (ECG), confirmed (persistent for \> 5 minutes) on repeated 12-lead ECGs;
* The occurrence of significant safety events that may pose a risk to subjects as judged by the SRC review; any adverse event(s) leading to subject withdrawal must be judged b

from Day 1 to Day 29

